        <mxCell id="business" value="&lt;font color=&#x27;#1A73E8&#x27;&gt;&lt;b style=&#x27;font-size:13px&#x27;&gt;Business Case&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;B2B E-Invoicing Mandate&lt;/b&gt;: Solves EN 16931 obligations (XRechnung, ZUGFeRD) under German UStG for freelancers, craft businesses, and SMEs.&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;Local-First Self-Hosting&lt;/b&gt;: Full data sovereignty on operator-owned hardware without SaaS subscriptions or cloud lock-in.&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;Integrated Document Store&lt;/b&gt;: RustFS provides local, S3-compatible storage designed for secure, long-term receipt archiving.&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;Open Architecture&lt;/b&gt;: Its open architecture supports integration with hybrid and S3-compatible cloud providers.&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;Lean TCO&lt;/b&gt;: Minimized operating and hardware costs via low-memory services designed for quiet mini PCs." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fontSize=10;fontColor=#202124;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#DADCE0;strokeWidth=2;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="90" width="1190" height="130" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="functional" value="&lt;font color=&#x27;#1A73E8&#x27;&gt;&lt;b style=&#x27;font-size:13px&#x27;&gt;Functional Overview&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;Master Data Management&lt;/b&gt;: Aggregates for issuers, recipients, items, B2B terms, and tax configurations.&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;Invoice Lifecycle&lt;/b&gt;: Strict state machine (draft, issued, cancelled) with atomic command-driven mutations.&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;Hybrid Invoice Generation&lt;/b&gt;: Asynchronous PDF/A-3b rendering and embedded ZUGFeRD/XRechnung XML synthesis.&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;Automated Validation&lt;/b&gt;: Multi-stage compliance checking via embedded KoSIT validator and Schematron rules.&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;Receipt &amp; Audit Vault&lt;/b&gt;: Checksum-based deduplication, structured expense tracking, and business reporting.&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;Mail Dispatch (optional)&lt;/b&gt;: Self-contained mail component — templates, SMTP submission, append-only send journal, signed archive package, journal-copy handover to the operator&#x27;s mail archive (ADR-037); off by default." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fontSize=10;fontColor=#202124;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#DADCE0;strokeWidth=2;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="230" width="290" height="220" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="context" value="&lt;font color=&#x27;#1A73E8&#x27;&gt;&lt;b style=&#x27;font-size:13px&#x27;&gt;Business Context&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;Office Manager / Owner&lt;/b&gt;: Edits master data, writes invoices, and tracks business receipts via the web UI.&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;Invoice Recipient&lt;/b&gt;: Receives legally compliant hybrid PDF/A-3b invoices and structured XML data (e-mail optional).&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;Tax Advisor / Auditor&lt;/b&gt;: Consumes GoBD-compliant e-invoice archives, receipt records, and export reports.&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;DevOps / Operator&lt;/b&gt;: Runs local server, manages backups, and configures TLS/systemd via operational scripts.&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;Out of Scope&lt;/b&gt;: Peppol AS4 routing, multi-tenant SaaS hosting, and double-entry accounting." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fontSize=10;fontColor=#202124;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#DADCE0;strokeWidth=2;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="340" y="230" width="490" height="450" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="context-img" value="" style="shape=image;html=1;verticalLabelPosition=bottom;verticalAlign=top;imageAspect=1;aspect=fixed;image=data:image/jpeg%3Bbase64,;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="350" y="400" width="470" height="270" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="org" value="&lt;font color=&#x27;#1A73E8&#x27;&gt;&lt;b style=&#x27;font-size:13px&#x27;&gt;Organizational Constraints&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;AI-Pair Development&lt;/b&gt;: Human architect directs strategy; autonomous AI coding agents implement and test.&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;Language Split&lt;/b&gt;: English technical codebase/architecture docs; German user-facing UI and business domain specifications.&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;Clean Licensing&lt;/b&gt;: Apache-2.0 software license; CC BY 4.0 attribution requirement for overall design concept.&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;Private Repository&lt;/b&gt;: Greenfield MVP (Minimum Viable Product); internal development workflow with decoupled releases.&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;Zero Skip Policy&lt;/b&gt;: Prohibited test skips (@Disabled, assumeTrue); all quality gates must pass cleanly." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fontSize=10;fontColor=#202124;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#DADCE0;strokeWidth=2;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="840" y="230" width="390" height="220" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="quality" value="&lt;font color=&#x27;#1A73E8&#x27;&gt;&lt;b style=&#x27;font-size:13px&#x27;&gt;Quality Goals&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;Domain Correctness (Legal &amp; Norm Conformance)&lt;/b&gt;: Strict EN 16931, UStG, and GoBD compliance verified prior to issuing invoices.&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;High-Assurance Testing &amp; Quality Gates&lt;/b&gt;: 90% line/branch JaCoCo gates, Karibu headless UI tests, and Playwright E2E suites.&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;Ergonomics &amp; Accessibility&lt;/b&gt;: German-first accessible UI (aria-labels, keyboard navigation, dark mode theme).&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;Operability on Small Hardware&lt;/b&gt;: Lean footprints, bounded memory budgets, restart resilience, and staged operations tooling.&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;Traceability &amp; Recovery&lt;/b&gt;: Reconstructable invoice lifecycle, audit trail, and age-encrypted backups.&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;Green-IT Resource Thrift&lt;/b&gt;: Size-budget policies, receipt downscaling at upload, and single-node energy efficiency." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fontSize=10;fontColor=#202124;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#DADCE0;strokeWidth=2;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="460" width="290" height="220" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="tech" value="&lt;font color=&#x27;#1A73E8&#x27;&gt;&lt;b style=&#x27;font-size:13px&#x27;&gt;Technical Constraints&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;Runtime Stack&lt;/b&gt;: Kotlin 2.x, JVM 25, Quarkus 3.x, Vaadin Flow 25, Typst layout engine (sole PDF layout engine).&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;Storage Foundation&lt;/b&gt;: PostgreSQL 18 (authoritative JPA store), Valkey (caching), RustFS (S3-compatible object store).&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;Event Backbone&lt;/b&gt;: NATS JetStream (generation jobs, maintenance events, mail requests/results via a frozen contract).&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;Container Standard&lt;/b&gt;: Multi-engine OCI compliance (Docker Engine, Podman, Colima, Rancher Desktop).&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;Deployment Topology&lt;/b&gt;: Single-node bare-metal Linux or mini PC; Caddy reverse proxy with automated TLS." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fontSize=10;fontColor=#202124;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#DADCE0;strokeWidth=2;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="840" y="460" width="390" height="220" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="hypotheses" value="&lt;font color=&#x27;#1A73E8&#x27;&gt;&lt;b style=&#x27;font-size:13px&#x27;&gt;Architecture Hypotheses&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;H1 (Modulith over Microservices)&lt;/b&gt;: Quarkus/Vaadin modulith plus two satellites — renderer (kotlin-xpdf) and optional mail SCS (kotlin-email) — minimizes ops overhead for single operators.&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;H2 (Lean Event Backbone)&lt;/b&gt;: NATS JetStream job envelopes with S3/Valkey payloads beat heavy brokers (Kafka) on small-budget hardware.&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;H3 (Strict Database Baselines)&lt;/b&gt;: Exactly two editable Flyway baselines (V1 schema, V2 seed) ensure deterministic greenfield deployments.&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;H4 (Out-of-Process Renderer)&lt;/b&gt;: Isolating PDFBox/Mustang rendering protects the interactive core web application from memory spikes.&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;H5 (Spec-First AI Delegation)&lt;/b&gt;: Strict architectural boundaries and ArchUnit quality gates sustain high agent-driven velocity." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fontSize=10;fontColor=#202124;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#DADCE0;strokeWidth=2;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="690" width="590" height="220" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="risks" value="&lt;font color=&#x27;#D93025&#x27;&gt;&lt;b style=&#x27;font-size:13px&#x27;&gt;Technical Challenges and Risks&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;Regulatory Churn&lt;/b&gt;: Frequent shifts in EN 16931, X-Rechnung profiles, and KoSIT Schematron release schedules.&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;Rendering Complexities&lt;/b&gt;: Dynamic page-break layout math, DIN 5008 precision on the sole Typst engine, and PDF/A-3b compliance.&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;Memory Constraints&lt;/b&gt;: Tight RAM limits (mini PC target) requiring aggressive garbage collection and lean caching.&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;UI Automation Overhead&lt;/b&gt;: Shadow-DOM and stateful Vaadin Flow lifecycles complicate resilient browser testing.&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;Single Maintainer / Bus Factor&lt;/b&gt;: High architectural leverage requires dense documentation and automated quality gates." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fontSize=10;fontColor=#202124;fillColor=#FCEEEE;strokeColor=#D93025;strokeWidth=3;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="640" y="690" width="590" height="220" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
